Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: aquantia: distinguish MDIO errors from an OFF timeout

phy_read_mmd_poll_timeout returns -ETIMEDOUT both when the positive OFF
status persists until the polling deadline and when the MDIO read itself
returns -ETIMEDOUT. Only the first case is an expected not-yet-ready
interface. Check the final register result before allowing that timeout.

Keep normal OFF handling, valid interface selection and rate adaptation.
Do not issue rate-register reads after an unsuccessful status-register
transaction, and preserve the original transport error for the caller.
This is a local follow-up to upstream 7e5b547cac7a, not an upstream patch.
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/aquantia/aquantia_main.c
@@ -360,6 +360,8 @@
 					AQR107_OP_IN_PROG_SLEEP,
 					AQR107_OP_IN_PROG_TIMEOUT, false);
+	if (val < 0)
+		return val;
 	if (ret && ret != -ETIMEDOUT)
 		return ret;
 
 	switch (FIELD_GET(MDIO_PHYXS_VEND_IF_STATUS_TYPE_MASK, val)) {
